>>__ load "simpLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `looper_ss`

``` hol4
simpLib.looper_ss : string * (simpLib.simpset -> tactic) ->
  simpLib.ssfrag
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Creates a fragment containing one looper.

Adding `looper_ss (name, mk)` to a simpset has the same effect as
`simpLib.add_looper (name, mk)`. The fragment is unnamed.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ss = simpLib.++ (boolSimps.bool_ss,
     simpLib.looper_ss ("conj", fn _ => CONJ_TAC));
```

### See also

[`simpLib.add_looper`](#simpLib.add_looper),
[`simpLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC`](#simpLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC).
